# cut_markers.manifest -- the "did the merged fix make the cut?" ledger.
#
# Every line is a fix MERGED to a source main that MUST be present in the
# about-to-be-cut artefact. scripts/verify_cut_provenance.sh reads this file and
# blocks the cut (gui/Makefile package + release.sh) if any marker is missing.
# When a new launch-blocking fix lands, add ONE line here -- every future cut is
# then gated on it. This is the mechanism that stops a merged-but-not-shipped fix
# (dead chat, 404 Doctor, unmerged same-org dupes) from recurring.
#
# Format (pipe-delimited, 4 fields):
#   kind | target | pattern | description
#
# kinds:
#   daemon_tag   target=<commit-sha>  pattern=<ignored>  -- the ostler-assistant
#                tag the daemon pin (gui/Makefile DAEMON_VERSION) resolves to MUST
#                contain this commit as an ancestor. Catches a stale daemon
#                tarball (pin says 0.4.8 but the v0.4.8 binary predates the fix).
#   vendor_file  target=<path-rel-CM051>  pattern=<ignored>  -- file must exist.
#   vendor_grep  target=<path-rel-CM051 file OR dir>  pattern=<regex>  -- pattern
#                must be present (grep -rE) under target.
#   assistant_tag_grep  target=<path-rel-ostler-assistant>  pattern=<regex>  --
#                pattern must appear in that file AT the daemon tag the pin
#                resolves to. Gates daemon-side / Hub-UI fixes with no vendored
#                footprint (the web bundle is rebuilt from source at cut time).
#   wiki_image_grep  target=<image-key>:<path-in-image>  pattern=<regex>  --
#                pulls the PINNED wiki Docker digest from install.sh
#                (image-key = wiki-site | wiki-compiler) and greps inside it.
#                FAIL-CLOSED: docker unavailable / pull fail = RED. Ends the
#                manual "did you rebuild the right wiki image" grep dance.
#
# --- v1.0.0 launch blockers (the v0.4.8 walk defects) ---
daemon_tag|383d021a|-|Mainline hub daemon (tag hub-v0.4.31 @ fa07f1c2 = hub-v0.4.30/7f585136 + #216). 383d021a = ratified mainline QR-fix anchor (CUT_PROVENANCE_CORRECTION_2026-07-08). RE-MEASURED 2026-10-14 (ORM): it IS an ancestor of hub-v0.5.16 in a full-history clone; the 'red on main' reading came from a SHALLOW 72-commit local checkout and was false. Ancestry is still blind to a future history rewrite, so the QR fix is also held by the two content rows below.
assistant_tag_grep|web/src/components/QrCode.tsx|^import QRCode from 'qrcode';|QR-fix CONTENT (held alongside the 383d021a ancestry anchor): the pairing QR is drawn by the qrcode library, not the broken vendored encoder. 0 at hub-v0.4.41 (pre-fix lineage, vendored web/src/lib/qr.ts present), 1 at hub-v0.5.16.
assistant_tag_absent|web/src/lib/qr.ts|-|QR-fix CONTENT: the broken vendored QR encoder is gone from the pinned tag. PRESENT at hub-v0.4.41, absent at hub-v0.5.16. Paired with the QrCode.tsx import row above.
assistant_tag_grep|crates/zeroclaw-providers/src/ollama.rs|Ollama model preloaded|#216 v1.0.9 recut: model-name-independent retry-on-empty + preload-model-on-config-reload (the "Ollama returned empty" chat-dead cure). Present only at hub-v0.4.31 (fa07f1c2); proves the recut daemon carries #216.
vendor_file|vendor/doctor/agent/duplicate_decision.py|-|#171 Doctor Same-person decision module (the 404 Save button)
vendor_grep|vendor/doctor/agent/web_ui.py|/api/v1/wiki/duplicates/decision|#171 Doctor decision route wired into web_ui
vendor_grep|vendor/cm041/identity_resolver|name_org_auto_merge|#40 resolver same-org auto-merge (the unmerged same-org dupes)
assistant_tag_grep|web/src/App.tsx|ReconnectingScreen|#566 passcode-flash fix (no 6-digit auto-render, calm reconnect)
assistant_tag_grep|web/src/pages/AgentChat.tsx|useIdentity|assistant chosen-name in chat (header + greeting via /api/identity)
wiki_image_grep|wiki-site:/docs/overrides|pwg-settling-bar|#84 REPLACEMENT: the REAL settling panel's CSS is baked into the pinned wiki-site image. The old row asserted 'pwg-hydration-temporary' -- the faked compile-time card Andy ordered removed after walking three DMGs with it. That row outlived the feature and turned this gate red against a correct image; CM044's own test_dashboard_hydration_panel.py now asserts .pwg-hydration is ABSENT, so the two checks were in direct contradiction.
wiki_image_absent|wiki-site:/docs/overrides|pwg-hydration[a-z-]*[[:space:]]*\{|#84 LOCK: no LIVE .pwg-hydration-* CSS rule may return to the shipped image ("I don't EVER want to see it again"). Matches a selector followed by an opening brace, so the two surviving deletion COMMENTS in extra.css do not trip it -- a bare "pwg-hydration" substring pattern did, which is why this one is brace-anchored. Validated both directions against the pinned image: 0 hits for pwg-hydration, 41 for the same shape on pwg-settling, so it really does detect live rules.
wiki_image_grep|wiki-site:/docs/overrides|padding-left: 1.4rem|#76/#623 card+admonition left-inset CSS baked into the pinned wiki-site image (the collapsed-padding cure: image serves extra.css from this dir)
wiki_image_grep|wiki-site:/docs/mkdocs.yml|^[[:space:]]*-[[:space:]]*navigation\.tabs\.sticky[[:space:]]*$|#876-class NAV CROP: the wiki nav bar Andy has reported cropped across ~10 DMGs. THE FIX IS NOT IN CSS. mkdocs-material's own JS hides the tab bar at 10px of scroll (m(({offset:{y:o}})=>({hidden: o>=10})) in bundle.d7400e89.min.js); the cure is the theme feature flag navigation.tabs.sticky, which takes the {hidden:!1} branch and moves the tabs inside .md-header. Anchored on the ENABLED LIST ITEM, not a bare substring: the same file carries the JS quoted in a comment at L65, so a loose 'navigation.tabs.sticky' pattern scores 2 and would stay green if the feature line were deleted -- a mention is not a setting. VALIDATED BOTH DIRECTIONS AGAINST THREE REAL PINNED IMAGES with the harness's own `grep -rq --` (BRE, not -E): 7d353848 (v1.0.38/40) NO MATCH, 0df14b72 (v1.0.41) MATCH, 0d3b46d5 (v1.0.43/44) MATCH. DO NOT anchor this on --ostler-md-header-h: it is present 5x in the PRE-fix 7d353848 image and 4x in the current one, so that row would have been GREEN on every cropped DMG. It belongs to the superseded FIX B, whose rule extra.css deletes on purpose.
wiki_image_grep|wiki-compiler:/app/compiler|_render_settling_panel|#84 REPLACEMENT: the honest settling-panel renderer is baked into the pinned wiki-compiler image (real mode = genuine done/total with a falling estimate; calendar mode = weighted burndown, no fabricated time). Supersedes the 'hydration_temporary' row, which asserted the presence of the deleted fake card.
wiki_image_absent|wiki-compiler:/app/compiler|hydration_temporary|#84 LOCK: the faked compile-time progress renderer must never return to the shipped image
wiki_image_grep|wiki-compiler:/app/compiler|duplicates/decision|#83 duplicates one-tap page in the pinned wiki-compiler image
wiki_image_grep|wiki-compiler:/app/compiler|inspect.signature|#85 SKIP_LLM signature-introspection dispatch in the pinned wiki-compiler image (old leak shape used a hardcoded name=="evernote"; its absence + this presence proves the baseline-compile gate ships)

